<div class="about-page">
    <section class="hero-copy about-intro"><span class="eyebrow">About FoodCare South Africa</span><h1>A practical digital starting point for food support.</h1><p class="lead">FoodCare is built around a South African problem: people can struggle to access enough nutritious food even when food exists in the wider economy. The platform aims to make support, information and opportunities to help easier to discover.</p></section>
    <div class="resource-grid">
        <article class="resource-card"><h3>Built around access</h3><p>The platform is not only about food production. It is about helping people navigate the support that may be available to them: social assistance, food banks, community organisations and donations.</p></article>
        <article class="resource-card"><h3>Built for South Africa</h3><p>Content uses South African terminology, provinces, social-support institutions, local organisations and the realities of household affordability and access.</p></article>
        <article class="resource-card"><h3>Built for dignity</h3><p>People looking for assistance should be able to find information without being made to feel that asking for support is a failure. The goal is practical, respectful access to help.</p></article>
    </div>
    <section class="content-section inner-section">
      <span class="eyebrow">The bigger picture</span><h2>Availability is not the same as food security.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Statistics South Africa's food-security work shows that South African households experience different levels of food insecurity. The 2023 figures report 19.7% of households experiencing moderate to severe food insecurity and 8.0% experiencing severe food insecurity.</p>
      <div class="cause-grid two-column"><div><h3>Economic pressure</h3><p>Food affordability is affected by household income, unemployment and the cost of living.</p></div><div><h3>Social support</h3><p>South Africa has a social-protection system and a large community and non-profit sector that can provide different forms of support.</p></div></div>
    </section>
</div>
</asp:Content>
